Read the knowledge base at the start of substantive work. Write findings there immediately (do not keep critical design only in chat).

## Quality bar

- Optimized hot paths; bounded storage; no significant idle load on constrained nodes.
- Unit tests for routing/secretary logic.
- Clear docs in `.cursor/client-base-project/` (README, use-cases, schemas as mermaid/text).
- Code clean and reviewable; minimal inline noise; contracts documented outside hot loops.

## Remotes

- `origin` = upstream `meshtastic/firmware` (fetch).
- `fork` = `c0dexter/firmware` (push feature branches).
- Do not commit secrets. Track `.cursor/` on this fork; omit from upstream PRs if reviewers prefer.
